---A technical cue or shot detection segment detected in a video. An array of SegmentDetection objects containing all segments detected in a stored video is returned by GetSegmentDetection.
---@class aws.rekognition.SegmentDetection
---@field Type? aws.rekognition.SegmentType The type of the segment. Valid values are TECHNICAL_CUE and SHOT.
---@field StartTimestampMillis aws.rekognition.Timestamp The start time of the detected segment in milliseconds from the start of the video. This value is rounded down. For example, if the actual timestamp is 100.6667 milliseconds, Amazon Rekognition Video returns a value of 100 millis.
---@field EndTimestampMillis aws.rekognition.Timestamp The end time of the detected segment, in milliseconds, from the start of the video. This value is rounded down.
---@field DurationMillis? aws.rekognition.ULong The duration of the detected segment in milliseconds.
---@field StartTimecodeSMPTE? aws.rekognition.Timecode The frame-accurate SMPTE timecode, from the start of a video, for the start of a detected segment. StartTimecode is in HH:MM:SS:fr format (and ;fr for drop frame-rates).
---@field EndTimecodeSMPTE? aws.rekognition.Timecode The frame-accurate SMPTE timecode, from the start of a video, for the end of a detected segment. EndTimecode is in HH:MM:SS:fr format (and ;fr for drop frame-rates).
---@field DurationSMPTE? aws.rekognition.Timecode The duration of the timecode for the detected segment in SMPTE format.
---@field TechnicalCueSegment? aws.rekognition.TechnicalCueSegment If the segment is a technical cue, contains information about the technical cue.
---@field ShotSegment? aws.rekognition.ShotSegment If the segment is a shot detection, contains information about the shot detection.
---@field StartFrameNumber? aws.rekognition.ULong The frame number of the start of a video segment, using a frame index that starts with 0.
---@field EndFrameNumber? aws.rekognition.ULong The frame number at the end of a video segment, using a frame index that starts with 0.
---@field DurationFrames? aws.rekognition.ULong The duration of a video segment, expressed in frames.

